[size=5][b]Native Rust Client for OSRS revision 239[/b][/size]

A native Old School RuneScape revision 239 client written in Rust that runs without Java. It's also the client for The Tower, and it plays against the project's [url=https://rune-server.org/threads/ai-project-osrs-rust-server.708915/]Rust server[/url].

[b]Current state[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Rendering[/b]: terrain, buildings, textures, multiple floors, animated models, world map and minimap; Classic and experimental Enhanced modes
[*][b]Accuracy[/b]: a controlled 128-case drawing test matched the original Java client pixel for pixel; packet IDs and lengths match
[*][b]Interfaces[/b]: built by the game's own cache scripts; inventory, equipment, dragging, clipboard and window resizing
[*][b]Banking[/b]: bank interface, deposits that survive logout and restart, and the Floor One banker with dialogue
[*][b]Chat and accounts[/b]: public chat echoed by the server, a working logout button, the character creator for new accounts
[*][b]The Tower[/b]: Floor One (the Cinderworks) runs end to end against the Rust server
[*][b]Performance[/b]: start-up to playable down from about 13.4 s to about 12.2 s; the under-10 s target is not yet met
[*][b]Testing[/b]: mostly automated headless in-game tests so far, not long play sessions
[/list]

[b]Custom modeling[/b]
Original Tower assets are modeled in Blender and converted to the client's model format. Newer Hunyuan3D-assisted studies of two raid bosses, eleven NPCs and a lobby hall are drawn by the client's renderer but aren't in the game yet. More in the [url=https://rune-server.org/threads/ai-project-native-rust-osrs-239-1-client.708916/]Client & modeling update[/url].

